+
+### 4.3 list_conversations
+
+The client requests its own conversation metadata with `list_conversations`; `limit` is an optional integer from 1 through 200, `before` is an optional cursor with an ISO `updatedAt` and a `sessionId`, both required together, and invalid fields receive `INVALID_MESSAGE` ([validated by: accepts a list request and rejects invalid limits or incomplete cursors](../../src/transport/conversationList.acceptance.test.ts#L105)).
+
+| Field              | Type   | Required | Description                   |
+| ------------------ | ------ | -------- | ----------------------------- |
+| `type`             | string | Yes      | `"list_conversations"`        |
+| `limit`            | number | No       | Integer from 1 through 200    |
+| `before.updatedAt` | string | No       | ISO activity time             |
+| `before.sessionId` | string | No       | Id tied to that activity time |
+
+The reply is one `conversation_list` of newest-first summaries containing only `sessionId`, `createdAt`, `updatedAt`, and `entryCount`, with both times as ISO strings; the server takes the user id from the authenticated connection, ignores any `userId` in the frame, passes the cursor through to the store, and a selected row can be reopened with `?sessionId=` when resume is enabled ([validated by: lists only the authenticated user’s summaries, pages on the wire cursor, and resumes a selected row](../../src/transport/conversationList.acceptance.test.ts#L136)).
+
+| Field                        | Type   | Description              |
+| ---------------------------- | ------ | ------------------------ |
+| `type`                       | string | `"conversation_list"`    |
+| `conversations`              | array  | One user's summaries     |
+| `conversations[].sessionId`  | string | Conversation id          |
+| `conversations[].createdAt`  | string | ISO creation time        |
+| `conversations[].updatedAt`  | string | ISO last activity time   |
+| `conversations[].entryCount` | number | Number of stored entries |
+
+`transport.history` is the deployer's opt-in decision to make a user's history reachable from the client; when absent or disabled, the request receives `UNSUPPORTED` and no list, while the retention bound remains the consumer's responsibility through the store's retention and erasure methods, as described in re-cinq/HALEngine#41 ([validated by: answers with UNSUPPORTED when history is not enabled](../../src/transport/conversationList.acceptance.test.ts#L172)).
+
+An enabled history request against a store without `listFor` receives `UNSUPPORTED`, never an empty list ([validated by: answers with UNSUPPORTED when an enabled store has no listFor](../../src/transport/conversationList.acceptance.test.ts#L182)).
+
+A list request is answered outside the per-session turn lock, so it can finish before a streaming turn's `stream_end` ([validated by: answers a list request before a streaming turn ends](../../src/transport/conversationList.acceptance.test.ts#L194)).
 
